export anchor EmberStyle:
    number: 318
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Ember
    idea: A calm fireside monitor on near black, where the day's traffic rises as a glowing ember curve, service cards warm from below, and one merged timeline of alerts, deploys and the incident reads like a log by the fire.
    base: dark
    palette:
        hearth: #0c0705, the page
        coal: #170e0a, the hero, service cards, chart cards and the style sheet
        coalRaised: #21140e, the incident card and list rows
        ink: #fbeee2, text
        ash: #caa995, meta, axis and labels
        sootLine: #3b261c, borders and grid
        ember: #ff7a3d, glows, the dotted p95 line, the current link underline, the foot of the primary button and the focus halo
        flame: #ffb347, the request line, p50, eyebrows, deploy marks and the focus outline
        deepRed: #b8321a, radial glows only, at low strength behind text
        healthy: #b8e68f, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
        degraded: #ffc857, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
        recovered: #e9c9a0, Recovered with a diamond
        firing: #ff7466, Firing with an octagon and the error line
    type:
        Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base 16px at
        1.55. The hero figure is 72px at 200, the incident ID 40px at 200,
        service uptimes 32px at 200, section titles 20px at 600, meta 13px.
    layout:
        A single centred 1040px column. A slim header holds a two tone
        flame mark, Brightwork Ops, the suite apps as plain text links at
        right with an ember underline on Ops, and a Production last 24 hours
        pill. The hero is a large 28px rounded card with a deep red bloom
        rising from its lower left. It reads Requests per minute, a huge
        light 9,400 with peak at the afternoon, a calm sentence about the
        quiet night and the current 7,700, then a full width area chart
        whose fill fades from flame to ember to deep red, with a pill
        marking the peak. Below, Services as five rounded cards whose
        bottoms glow warmer for services that need attention, each with the
        name, an outline status shape and word, a light uptime figure and
        one fact. Then two columns, a glowing incident card with INC-0427
        and its facts and buttons, and Since last night, one merged timeline
        newest first of deploys, billing recovered, alerts and the incident
        opening, each with its own shape. Last, two cards for Error rate and
        Latency. Below 960px the two columns stack, below 760px cards go two
        across with billing full width.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter, 48px between blocks, 20 to 36px inside cards.
    density: Roomy. One hero chart, five cards, two blocks and two small charts in a 1040px column.
    corners: Soft. 28px hero and sheet, 20 to 24px cards, 14px buttons and fields, round pills.
    borders: 1px soot lines. The incident card has a deeper red brown border.
    shadows: Warm glows instead of drop shadows. A low orange bloom under the hero and incident, a 6px glow on the request line.
    icons:
        Few. A two tone flame mark. Status as outline circle, triangle and
        diamond on cards, filled square, octagon and diamond in the
        timeline, an arrow on a base for deploys, always with the word.
    focus: A 2px flame outline offset 3px plus a soft ember halo.
    tone: Calm and warm, such as Since last night, Quiet through the night and 7,700 now.
